<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!DOCTYPE plist PUBLIC "-//Apple//DTD PLIST 1.0//EN" "http://www.apple.com/DTDs/PropertyList-1.0.dtd">
<!--
  Keep Voice Memos.app running, because iCloud syncs it ONLY while it runs.

  ⚠ THIS IS THE WHOLE IN-PERSON MEETING DOOR, AND IT CLOSED SILENTLY.

  Measured 2026-10-25: `CloudRecordings.db-wal` had not been touched since
  Oct 19 06:37 and Voice Memos.app was not running on the Studio. Six days of
  memos recorded on the phone never reached the box. Messages and Notes were
  both up, so their doors were fine; this one was shut by nothing more than an
  app having been quit at some point.

  The sweep DOES detect it — it prints "The snapshot is NNNh old ... or Voice
  Memos.app is closed on the Studio" in its own log notes, and `probeVoiceMemos`
  reports it on /settings/health. Neither is a channel anybody reads on a given
  morning, and Pepper's outbound notes are held (CLAUDE.md §13), so the
  detection was correct and the outcome was still six lost days.

  ⚠ A CHANNEL WHOSE SETUP CANNOT BE AUTOMATED IS A CHANNEL THAT IS OFF (§12 —
  Pepper's own text transport proved it over seven days of `Couldn't find
  shortcut`). "Remember to leave Voice Memos open" is exactly that kind of
  manual step, so it is replaced with a KeepAlive rather than documented.

  KeepAlive + RunAtLoad: launchd reopens the app within seconds of it being
  quit or crashing, and at login. `-g` keeps it from stealing focus, so the
  window never jumps in front of whatever is on the Studio's displays.

  ⚠ Notes.app deliberately has NO equivalent agent. It was running at the time
  of the measurement and its WAL was current, so adding one would be a fix for a
  problem nobody has observed — and §12's standing instruction is to measure
  before building. If the notes sweep ever reports a stale snapshot while this
  one is fresh, that is the evidence, and the agent is a copy of this file.
-->
<plist version="1.0">
<dict>
  <key>Label</key><string>com.berwilson.voicememos-keeper</string>
  <key>ProgramArguments</key>
  <array>
    <string>/usr/bin/open</string>
    <string>-g</string>
    <string>-W</string>
    <string>-b</string>
    <string>com.apple.VoiceMemos</string>
  </array>
  <key>RunAtLoad</key><true/>
  <key>KeepAlive</key><true/>
  <!--
    `open -W` waits for the app to exit, so launchd sees a long-running process
    and KeepAlive restarts it when the app quits. Without -W, open returns
    immediately, KeepAlive sees a process that exits at once, and launchd
    throttles the job as a crash loop — which is a keeper that keeps nothing.

    ⚠ `-b <bundle id>` AND NOT `-a "Voice Memos"`. The first version used the
    display name and failed with `Unable to find application named 'Voice
    Memos'` — the bundle is `/System/Applications/VoiceMemos.app`, with no space.
    §12 in miniature: a vendor's NAME is a UI string, not an API contract, and
    `com.apple.VoiceMemos` is the identifier that survives a rename or a
    localisation. Found by checking the keeper's own error log rather than by
    assuming the load had worked, because launchd reported the job LOADED either
    way — a job that is loaded and failing looks exactly like one that is
    working.
  -->
  <key>ThrottleInterval</key><integer>30</integer>
  <key>StandardOutPath</key><string>__LOG_DIR__/voicememos-keeper.log</string>
  <key>StandardErrorPath</key><string>__LOG_DIR__/voicememos-keeper.err.log</string>
</dict>
</plist>
